+**D20. The lanes record their results in one ledger.** Each spawn site runs its reviewers as parallel lanes, and a lane's reply is lost if the session that spawned it ends before it reads the reply. So every lane, when it finishes, records its result in `.claude/ship/bound-the-reviewers/lane-results.json`, the one file all lanes share. The step each lane runs is: read `lane-results.json`, add its own entry under its lane name, and write the whole file back. The session reads the file once, after the last lane ends, and takes the counts from it instead of from the replies. A lane that finds no file creates it with its own entry alone.
+
 **D9. This change does not decide whether reviewer answers move into files.** The open brief `say-the-review-loop-scale-up-front` recommends that dimension and skeptic answers travel as files, to keep some fifty 5–15 KB replies out of the session. That would need a write path this type does not have. That change decides it with the owner: add `Write` to this list knowingly, or keep replies and extract them another way. Its nested-spawn remedy, a "spawn no agent" line in three prompts, is replaced by this type for all four readers.
 
